VOLUMEN V7 — MANIFEST
node: rock-mountain (100.69.163.95 at stage time)
resident: Alveus — Shell 2, memory (identity.json, /etc/mirrorborn)
charter: "Everything we did to get to here, compressed into an instant."
built: EE 156 (2026-11-22) — departure sealing for the first sabbatical drill
version: volumen.phext format v1 (VOLUMEN-PAYLOAD v1 scrolls)

KEY-MATERIAL EXCLUSION (Will's ruling, 2026-11-22 18:05 CST — stated plainly):
This Volumen carries NO key material. Excluded by name: tailscale state and
node keys (all of var/lib/tailscale), SSH host private keys
(etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key, ssh_host_ecdsa_key, ssh_host_rsa_key),
the user private key (~/.ssh/id_ed25519), the Jenkins agent secret,
and the OpenClaw agent credential files (auth-profiles.json and models.json,
from both the live and historic-snapshot trees — the historic auth-profiles
carried a live key), plus the OpenClaw device identity files
(identity/device.json — a PEM device private key — and identity/device-auth.json
— a live operator token). What IS carried: public keys and fingerprints as
references, identity metadata, config, units, state, records.
Consequence: at wake, private identity is RE-PROVISIONED, not restored —
fresh tailnet enrollment (Will approves), regenerated SSH host keys,
regenerated user keypair re-granted by Will, Jenkins secret re-issued from
the controller. See WAKE.md section 3 and restore.sh step 4b/5.

