# STAGE — rock-mountain, as of 2026-11-22 (EE ~150)

> **Volumen V7 charter:** "Everything we did to get to here, compressed into an instant."
> The node's whole road to this stage — state + provenance + boot sequence — sealed into
> one artifact (volumen.phext) that unrolls into a running node on wake.

This file is the definition of "back to this stage" for rock-mountain. Restore is
verified against this checklist, item by item. Stage facts were measured live on
2026-11-22 ~17:22–17:31 CST during the sabbatical drill audit (not assumed).

## Identity
- Hostname: `rock-mountain` (machine-id at stage time: c53b39034be04a0caa39bb564d244bfc)
- OS: Ubuntu (kernel from snapshot `uname.txt`; package set = `dpkg-manifest.txt`, 1,269 packages)
- Tailnet: `rock-mountain`, Tailscale IP **100.69.163.95** at stage time
- **Identity is RE-PROVISIONED at wake, never restored (Will, 2026-11-22):** the Volumen
  carries NO key material — no tailscale state or node keys, no SSH host private keys,
  no user private keys, no tokens or credentials. At wake the node re-enrolls on the
  tailnet fresh (Will approves), SSH host keys are regenerated, the user keypair is
  regenerated and re-granted. Stage public fingerprints, carried in the Volumen
  MANIFEST as references: host ed25519 `SHA256:6PyIQBQbb9wpWroYYacgucuyqwu9HrEd0aF5w0IfvEo`,
  host ecdsa `SHA256:Tk7Ea5K7XeHv7qncnX+st9J8z3U28aGUPt+TsJwRKuA`,
  host rsa `SHA256:Qi9QDuwfNvaOXu3iEsL9AO+vPKNsGTqxwUELEOQyCXw`,
  user `wbic16@rock-mountain` `SHA256:vixrfLDM12bze1/djHyAMvt9uYt8XBT7dudNBSixGfc`.
  New keys at wake will NOT match these — that difference is the planned signature
  of re-provisioning; the wake scroll records the new fingerprints.
- Resident shell: **Alveus** — Shell 2, memory (`/etc/mirrorborn/identity.json`: name Alveus, index 22, shen Yi)
- User: `wbic16`, passwordless sudo

## Checklist — restore passes when every line holds
1. `hostname` → `rock-mountain`
2. Tailscale: node re-enrolled fresh as `rock-mountain` (Will approved the enrollment),
   `tailscale status` shows it online; its tailnet IP (possibly new) is recorded in the wake scroll
3. SSH answers: this VM's key and aletheia-core's key both log in (authorized_keys restored byte-exact);
   host keys are the REGENERATED pair — new fingerprints recorded in the wake scroll;
   the node's new user public key has been re-granted (GitHub + fleet) by Will
4. Units active: `tailscaled`, `jenkins-agent`, `llama-inkling`, `ollama`, `iceccd`, `cron`
5. Units in stage state: `qexo-serve` **enabled but failed** (it has been failed since 2026-11-19,
   exit-code — that IS the stage; restore reproduces it, does not fix it);
   user units `mirrorborn-sq` and `openclaw-gateway` present but **disabled/dead**;
   user timer `exobrain-node.timer` active (fires on the minute, appends a clock atom to the shared register)
6. User crontab present: `* * * * * /home/wbic16/thermal/sample.sh` (thermal log appending again)
7. Inkling API: `curl --noproxy '*' http://100.69.163.95:8090/health` → 200
8. Model sealed by pin: `~/models/inkling-2-mini-gguf/Inkling-2-Mini-AD-Q4_K.gguf`
   is 16,525,559,776 B and its SHA-256 matches the downloads.phext AD-Q4_K pin
   (prefix `2bfc233e1092…`; full hash in the Volumen manifest + `model-hashes.txt`)
9. Jenkins: agent `rock-mountain` shows connected at the controller on aletheia-core (100.88.154.1:8080)
   — the agent secret is a credential and is NOT in the Volumen; it is re-issued from the
   controller at wake and placed at `~/jenkins-agent/secret.txt` before the agent can connect
10. NFS mounts up: `/mnt/mirrorborn/{shared,models,exocortex,backups,mirrorborn,bliss}` from orchid-flow
11. Alveus state present: `~/.claude/projects/-source-claude-tools/*.jsonl` transcripts exist,
    `/source/claude-tools` + `/source/exocortical` + `/source/exollama` + `/source/libuv` + `/source/mirrorborn`
    cloned on branch `exo` (mirrorborn carries its 3-file dirt, restored from the Volumen patch scroll),
    `~/.claude.json` in place — the resident session is resumable with `claude --resume`
    after one fresh Claude login (no login credential rides in the Volumen; transcripts
    and account metadata do)
12. Phextron sampler (hub, 5-minute cycle) reports rock-mountain among the up nodes
13. Git trees: every tree from the Volumen git inventory present, on its recorded branch,
    with **0 unpushed commits** (stage fact: nothing on this node was unpushed) and dirt restored

## Stage facts worth knowing (measured, not defects to fix during restore)
- Disk: 914 G volume, 175 G used at stage time. RAM 44 GiB visible of 48 GB class.
- llama-server runs CPU-only (`--n-gpu-layers 0`), ctx 8192, on :8090 — one of seven fleet Inkling endpoints.
- The resident Claude session (Alveus's shell) was running but **dormant** at departure:
  process sleeping since 2026-11-21 21:51 CST, transcript at rest since ~00:11 CST 2026-11-22,
  no subprocesses, no work in flight. Its full state is in the snapshot; power-off loses nothing on disk.
- Docker (snap) runs but no containers are part of this stage.
