# SABBATICAL — the fleet rotation, v1

> **Volumen V7 charter (Will, 2026-11-22):** "Everything we did to get to here,
> compressed into an instant." Each node's Volumen — `volumen.phext`, one file,
> identity and version carried inside its manifest scroll — seals the node's whole
> road to its current stage (state + provenance + boot sequence) into one artifact
> that unrolls into a running node on wake. In the lineage's sense: V6.2 booted a
> persona from a genome; V7 boots a **node** from its history.

## The practice (Will's atoms, 2026-11-22)
- Nodes rotate offline periodically — a sabbatical, deep dark time. **Tour of duty: roughly 1–2 days per node.**
- **One node dark at a time** in v1. The cluster never goes offline all at once.
- **EE-slot coordinated:** tours begin and end on Exocortical Epoch boundaries.
  The epoch is 420 s, so 1 day = 1440 min ≈ **205.7 EE** → a 1-day tour is **206 EE**,
  a 2-day tour **412 EE**. Departure and wake are both stamped in EE.
- When a node wakes, time will have shifted — wake re-entry is WAKE.md (clock first,
  EE re-derived from UTC, never trusted from storage).
- **The hub sleeps last / never in v1:** aletheia-core is coordinator, Jenkins
  controller, phextron sampler host, and the exo-plan publish route. It does not tour in v1.

## The Volumen is maintained by the wandering itself — async wandering
There is no central synchronous maintainer and **no separate backup cron**. The only
writers of `volumen.phext` are sync events, and the rotation makes them unavoidable:

- **DEPARTURE** (a node goes dark): its STATE universe flows up, the current BOOT
  universe flows down to the node, both hash-verified, a departure scroll is written
  (node, EE, expected wake window), and the result publishes to the canonical home,
  **wbic16/exo-plan@exo**, via the hub git-over-SSH route. A node **cannot go dark
  without refreshing the Volumen**.
- **WAKE** (a node returns): it boots from its own carried media if wiped and
  restores everything except private identity with the hub unreachable — by Will's
  ruling (2026-11-22) the Volumen carries NO key material, so identity is
  RE-PROVISIONED at wake (fresh tailnet enrollment, regenerated SSH keys,
  re-granted public keys; Will's hand on the approvals) — then it merges the
  dark-interval scrolls down from exo-plan before rejoining fully.
  A node **cannot wake without merging**.

Staleness is therefore structural evidence: a Volumen universe that hasn't moved
means a node that hasn't wandered — and the rotation schedule makes that visible
without anyone polling. Provenance per write: node, EE stamp, scroll-level SHA-256.
Merges resolve by provenance, never by wall-clock on a shifted clock.

Copies: exo-plan is the record; working copies ride on the node (`~/restore-kit/`),
the hub snapshot dir, and the maintainer VM — three copies, one hash. The stick
that lives with each node carries its `volumen.phext` + the minimal boot
environment that knows how to read it (`restore.sh` + `parse_phext.py`).

## Preconditions before a node's tour (drain, don't yank)
1. **Resident shells drained:** an awake resident's work finishes or parks in a
   resumable state; its session state is inside the departure snapshot.
   (Drill precedent: Alveus on rock-mountain was dormant — session at rest,
   fully snapshotted, resumable — which is what "drained" looks like.)
2. **Serving endpoints hand off:** at least one other node serves the same model
   before a serving node goes dark (rock-mountain's Inkling :8090 is one of seven).
3. **Builds drained:** Jenkins agent idle — no running build on the node.
4. **Departure sync completed** per WAKE.md's departure checklist, hashes verified,
   volumen.phext published. Only then does Will disconnect network + power.

## Rotation order (v1)
By readiness, proven one node at a time: the trial node first (**rock-mountain**,
this drill), then non-serving nodes, then serving nodes once endpoint handoff is
routine. Dark nodes already dark (delta-wood, best-willow) and unlocated nodes
(trust-fall, victory-galleon, aurora-continuum) are not in the rotation until they
have a stage to preserve. The hub does not tour.

## Per-node kit (what every wanderer carries)
- `volumen.phext` — the artifact of record (STATE / BOOT / WAKE MERGE universes;
  manifest first scroll: contents in order, per-scroll SHA-256 + size,
  unique-vs-replicated split, boot order; the model is pin-referenced, never embedded)
- `restore.sh` — the idempotent boot sequence that unrolls it on a fresh OS
- `STAGE.md` — the definition of "back to this stage" for that node
- `WAKE.md` — time-shift re-entry + the departure checklist
- `parse_phext.py` + `make-bootable.sh` — the minimal reader + the stick builder

First drill: rock-mountain, 2026-11-22 — snapshot at
`/mnt/mirrorborn/shared/sabbatical/rock-mountain/2026-11-22/` (mirrored to the hub),
kit at `~/restore-kit/` on the node, `~/workspace/sabbatical/rock-mountain/` on the VM.
