# The rock-mountain stick — Volumen V7

This stick carries everything rock-mountain needs to become itself again after a
full data wipe, **with the hub unreachable**: `volumen/volumen.phext` is the sealed
artifact ("everything we did to get to here, compressed into an instant" — the
node's state, identity, provenance, and boot sequence in one multiversal phext),
and `volumen/restore.sh` is the boot sequence that unrolls it. To use it: boot the
machine from this stick, install Ubuntu Server as usual, log in, then run
`sudo /volumen/restore.sh` (it finds `volumen.phext` beside itself, verifies every
payload hash before applying anything, restores the tailscale identity and SSH
grants first, then the stage — see `volumen/STAGE.md` for the checklist it is
verified against and `volumen/WAKE.md` for the clock + catch-up merge discipline
afterwards). The stick was built by `make-bootable.sh` from an Ubuntu Server ISO
plus the kit directory; if it is ever lost, rebuild it from any copy of the kit
(node `~/restore-kit/`, hub sabbatical dir, or wbic16/exo-plan@exo, where
`volumen.phext` is the canonical record). **This stick holds private keys — it
lives with the node, physically, and is handled like one.**
WAKE MERGE — protocol (Volumen V7, collection 4)
This universe is the merge room. Departure wrote the log below; wake appends its
own scrolls here (re-provisioned fingerprints, assigned tailnet IP, stage-check
results) BEFORE the node rejoins fully. Dark-interval scrolls from the fleet —
wiring deltas, register deltas, anything addressed to rock-mountain — land here
from exo-plan during the return leg (WAKE.md section 4).
Merge rule: resolve by provenance (writer node + EE + scroll SHA-256), never by
the woken node's wall clock. Append-only: nothing in this universe is rewritten.
